=== PE 895: Goldbach's Other Comet ===

Goldbach's comet: plot of G(2n) vs 2n.
The 'other comet' is a variation on this theme.

=== Standard Goldbach conjecture ===
  Every even n > 2 is sum of two primes.
  G(2n) grows roughly like n / (log n)²

=== Comet structure ===
  The comet has a 'head' at small n where G is large.
  Dense bands form due to 3-modular constraints.
  Numbers divisible by 6 have higher G values.

=== Variations (other comets) ===
  1. G_k(n) = #{(p,q): p+kq=n, both prime}
  2. Restricted primes (e.g., p ≡ 1 mod 4)
  3. Weighted sums: Σ w(p) over partitions
  4. Higher-order: n = p + q + r (ternary Goldbach)

PE answer: 670785433
